{"created": "2026-09-27T15:55:59.681754+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-06T02:00:53.785070+00:00", "id": 22999133, "conceptrecid": "22967098", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22999133", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22967098", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22999133", "metadata": {"title": "Supporting data and code for \"Two Transit-like Signals in TESS Photometry of the Nearby K Dwarf TIC 4206066\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22999133", "publication_date": "2026-09-27", "description": "<p>Supporting research materials for the manuscript \"Two Transit-like Signals in TESS Photometry of the Nearby K Dwarf TIC 4206066\" by Pavel Rabtsevich. The study examines TESS photometry from Sectors 6, 32, and 98 and reports a 3.18-day planet candidate and a tentative 11.13-day transit-like signal. The host of the 3.18-day signal remains uncertain, with an unresolved bound companion remaining an alternative. No statistical validation is claimed. The upload consists of README.md and three ZIP archives containing the supporting materials (input product list, per-transit measurements, the archival recovery test, the TRICERATOPS false-positive runs and their decomposition by companion mass, companion limits, pixel localisation, the 11.13-day analysis, the data behind Figure 1, and software environments). Data and documentation: CC BY 4.0; original code: MIT; third-party materials keep their original terms (see README.md).</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Rabtsevich, Pavel", "affiliation": "Independent Researcher", "orcid": "0009-0005-0654-6658"}], "keywords": ["TESS", "TIC 4206066", "transit photometry", "exoplanet candidates", "false-positive analysis"], "version": "1.0.1", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22967098"}}]}}, "title": "Supporting data and code for \"Two Transit-like Signals in T